{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf","id":1000986,"title":"Love and Sex in Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-09T14:33:17-08:00","id":1000986,"title":"Love and Sex in Werewolf","content":"I was wondering how important love and consensual sex are in your Werewolf games? I often use love and sex for creating plot hooks and, quite frankly, I enjoy using the emotions from the discussions about love and sex to make my games memorable. I think that both love and consensual sex are stabilizing factors for Werewolves, so I reduce effective Rage by one for rolling for frenzy and for determining the effects of the Curse within 24 hours after consensual sex, when they are loved by their parents, when they are loved by their partners, when they are loved by their children (all four effects are cumulative). It makes Kinfolk especially important because parents, partners, and children can be Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:11:36-08:00","id":1001018,"title":"","content":"I personally don't see a reason to come up with a system effect for a Garou's sex life.<br /> <br /> By your system, any Garou with a few points in the Kinfolk background is all but guaranteed to never have to worry about Frenzy or the Curse. That is just an initial thought though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:19:28-08:00","id":1001023,"title":"","content":"Well, you do not automatically gain the love of your Kinfolk. I find that it gives Garou a mechanical reason to be positively involved in the lives of their Kinfolk, which tends to be lacking in a Werewolf game. It also means that Garou without Kinfolk will be seen by Garou society as loose cannons, as they will have unchecked Rage. I would suggest that Garou who engage in rape and mistreat their Kinfolk receive a penalty in the form of dice added to their Rage for rolling for frenzy and for determining the effects of the Curse. Garou who regularly rape civilians, beat their partners and children, and torment their parents would increase their effective Rage by four for the purposes of rolling for frenzy and determining the Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:42:54-08:00","id":1001094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001023#post1001023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find that it gives Garou a mechanical reason to be positively involved in the lives of their Kinfolk, which tends to be lacking in a Werewolf game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn't need a crunchy carrot to have well-rounded characters. If players aren't fleshing out their in-game proxies to an adequate degree, that is hardly the fault of the system for not bribing them.<br /> <br /> You don't need penalties for rape either. If a player starts having their Garou rape people, the fix for that is to avoid play with them altogether, not hit them with dice penalties (???).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:57:06-08:00","id":1001101,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a>, rape shouldn't bring dice pool penalties. If you have a problem with player going around raping in game, put a stop to that. Either by talking to the player or getting them out of your group.<br /> <br /> In any case, on the positives side, I suppose I can see why you set up that system, to encourage players to interact more with their kinfolk. I just don't think players should have to be bribed to have good relationships with their family.<br /> <br /> Oh...in setting though, I suppose they already do. There is Renown awarded for maintaining good relations with kin. Failing everything else, that should incentivize the players (I also seem to remember a penalty for failing to do so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":".  Added the Renown bit 11-09-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:42:42-08:00","id":1001272,"title":"","content":"The &quot;kinfolk is affected by the Curse to a lesser degree&quot; statement usually, works in my games in a way that kinfolk show no effects of the Curse within a time period that is suitable within the context of the game. So it can be up to a few weeks or so if the Garou comes home from a long umbra quest or something like that and wants and needs to spend time with his loved ones.<br /> <br /> That said, whenever there is a kinfolk character around in the LARP games, all Garou characters get really flirty, especially if they don't have a kinfolk partner already. Rape or any other form of non-consensual sex is usually limited to a theme of something that happened to NPCs or in character background stories. Rarely there are Garou offenders/Kin victim scenarios in character background stories, so it seems most players don't see that as common.<br /> <br /> We don't attribute any special rules to any love or relationship scenario unless the True Love Merit is involved. There is, however, an ongoing discussion about whether a mother would kill her toddler child in a frenzy. A point we as STs have kept vague so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:30:38-08:00","id":1001366,"title":"","content":"I would actually suggest that a mother would not kill their child in a frenzy unless the mother's Rage exceeded the mother's Willpower or the mother's Gnosis, but that is just my call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:55:23-08:00","id":1001392,"title":"","content":"Human mothers kill their babies accidently (and sometimes on purpose) without a Rage attribute or Frenzy condition. I would be hesitant to have a built in safeguard for that sort of thing for Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:08:42-08:00","id":1001420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001392#post1001392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human mothers kill their babies accidently (and sometimes on purpose) without a Rage attribute or Frenzy condition. I would be hesitant to have a built in safeguard for that sort of thing for Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, toss in it also makes kin all the more valuable. Kin can't frenzy so at times a parent garou would need to back away for the safety of the child, and allow someone without that risk to care for them. To me it helps make Gaia'so plan of having the garou need kin for family all the more visceral.<br /> <br /> Also Some players won't mind a renown hit for mating with another garou or even other fera, but if there is a risk of frenzy induced infanticide...things change a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:18:07-08:00","id":1001485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001420#post1001420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also Some players won't mind a renown hit for mating with another garou or even other fera, but if there is a risk of frenzy induced infanticide...things change a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>A renown hit for breaking the Litany? Pretty sure that player's guts would be bunting at the next moot if they mated with other Garou.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:21:45-08:00","id":1001487,"title":"","content":"Maybe for some, but the books have painted a less lethal view of breaking that tenet..since you can take it as a flaw in character creation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:35:57-08:00","id":1001494,"title":"","content":"The punishment is still further reaching than a simple Renown hit.<br /> <br /> And how is gets reacted to has a lot to do with Tribe and edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:39:19-08:00","id":1001499,"title":"","content":"We could also be using different mind sets when I say &quot;reknown hit&quot;. I don't mean just a slap on the hand like -2 wisdom or something like that. I more mean to some of the player's I've known, punishment rites don't deter them because they get to have that whole &quot;the world can't handle our love&quot; thing...but when you toss in that they could take a nip from their little metis and lose their mind reducing their bundle of joy to a bundle of giblets...they didn't want to do it anymore.<br /> <br /> For example: I played (note: Played, not ran) in a game where an NPC Silver Fang and a Corax PC became a couple and had a baby...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:40:23-08:00","id":1001525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001499#post1001499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We could also be using different mind sets when I say &quot;reknown hit&quot;. I don't mean just a slap on the hand like -2 wisdom or something like that. I more mean to some of the player's I've known, punishment rites don't deter them because they get to have that whole &quot;the world can't handle our love&quot; thing...but when you toss in that they could take a nip from their little metis and lose their mind reducing their bundle of joy to a bundle of giblets...they didn't want to do it anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> I think maybe I just had carryover from another thread and wanted to head off the &quot;it's just -2 Wisdom&quot; mindset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001499#post1001499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For example: I played (note: Played, not ran) in a game where an NPC Silver Fang and a Corax PC became a couple and had a baby...</div> </div> </div> </div>In setting, at least that's not against the Litany. It's <i>just</i> a generally dangerous situation for a kid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:43:33-08:00","id":1001526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001499#post1001499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I played (note: Played, not ran) in a game where an NPC Silver Fang and a Corax PC became a couple and had a baby...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I think that is a horse of a different color. That sounds politically dangerous because Silver Fangs are typically obsessed with who they breed with, but Fera + Garou couplings are generally more favorable than Garou + Garou pairings, right? Doesn't that just lead to a kinfolk child, anyway? Corax parents have to perform a funky egg rite to make more of themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":"get outta my head, idpersona! 11-10-2016, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:46:35-08:00","id":1001556,"title":"","content":"Yeah, anything can breed with Corax (except for Kuei-jin and 15th generation Kindred) and just get Corax Kinfolk. If two Fera reproduce, they just produce Kinfolk or a Fera who is also Kinfolk with another breed of Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T17:48:46-08:00","id":1001557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001392#post1001392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human mothers kill their babies accidently (and sometimes on purpose) without a Rage attribute or Frenzy condition. I would be hesitant to have a built in safeguard for that sort of thing for Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but at the same time unless there was a very special story/plot I wanted to run, it wouldn't happen either in any of my chronicles. And I can't see myself ever doing it to a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T18:52:08-08:00","id":1001584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1000986-love-and-sex-in-werewolf?p=1001557#post1001557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"